  "description": "of the fleet-the model that\nstarted Fuji's foray into mountain bike making in 1983. It's the pointed\nend of 19 years of research and development.\n\nThe heart of this beast is its X-Fusion Alpha frame. It's not just light.\nIt's not just strong. It's a revolutionary new aluminum alloy. That means\nin addition to the elements that make up aluminum alloy, there are \"ceramic\ninclusions\" that allow the tubes to be radically shaped (such as\nthe biaxially ovalized PowerDiamond downtube and custom-tapered/butted\nTrailTuned seat- and chain stays) without compromising strength. But that's\nnot all. There's a secret ingredient that causes the grain structure to\nrealign after welding. Translation: It's really strong stuff that allows\nwelds, so you don't have to use a whole lot of it. The result is one incredibly\nlight, incredibly strong frame that climbs hills, slithers through singletrack,\nand carves descents better than your wildest dreams.\n\nDon't dilly-dally over this one. Fuji only makes a few and they sell out\nquickly. The Mt. Fuji is available as a frame alone, or built into a 21-pound\nwonderbike that'll leave the rest of the crowd wondering how you got out\nof sight so fast and if you'll be kind enough to wait up any time soon.\nI say let 'em wonder.",
